<title>SWEDEN: Riksbank ends board meeting, no rate changes.</title>
<headline>Riksbank ends board meeting, no rate changes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, on Wednesday ended its regular board meeting without announcing any changes to its key interest rates.</p>
<p>No rate changes were expected.  </p>
<p>The central bank's lending and deposit rates currently stand at 5.25 percent and 3.75 percent, respectively. The repurchase rate is set at 4.10 percent.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
